Autoscaling groups automatically adjust the number of Instances based on metrics like CPU or memory usage.
This allows you to automatically scale your infrastructure up or down to meet demand while optimizing costs.

USAGE:
  scw autoscaling group <command>

AVAILABLE COMMANDS:
  create      Create an autoscaling group
  delete      Delete an autoscaling group
  get         Get an autoscaling group
  list        List autoscaling groups
  update      Update an autoscaling group

FLAGS:
  -h, --help                help for group
      --list-sub-commands   List all subcommands

GLOBAL FLAGS:
  -c, --config string    The path to the config file
  -D, --debug            Enable debug mode
  -o, --output string    Output format: json or human, see 'scw help output' for more info (default "human")
  -p, --profile string   The config profile to use

Use "scw autoscaling group [command] --help" for more information about a command.
